<body>
    <h1>PTF - RAP Access</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <div role=3D"region" aria-label=3D"Info" class=3D"confluence-inform=
ation-macro  confluence-information-macro-information">
 <p class=3D"title conf-macro-render">Rollout session</p><span role=3D"pres=
entation" class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-info-filled conflue=
nce-information-macro-icon"></span>
 <div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
  <p>Rollout Session from Tuesday, Aug 2 2022: recording linked at <a href=
=3D"https://wiki.one.int.sap/wiki/display/SimplSuite/Process+Test+Framework=
?src=3Dcontextnavpagetreemode" rel=3D"nofollow">Main page</a></p>
 </div>
</div>
<h3 id=3D"PTFRAPAccess-Introduction">Introduction</h3>
<p>PTF can also be used to directly access any RAP BO - without writing any=
 ABAP code or using any PTF BO class.</p>
<p>The value helps for BO and Action offer additionally all existing RAP BO=
s from this system and their available actions.</p>
<p><br></p>
<p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-manu=
al-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image" draggable=3D"false" width=
=3D"440" src=3D"72173001e00948eca7e6ab27263b375070fd5ce3f3980dc6bc36b380422=
da476" data-image-src=3D"/wiki/download/attachments/2966325080/image2022-8-=
1_20-20-4.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1659378005000&amp;api=3Dv2=
" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"3046509919=
" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachmen=
t" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image2022-8-1_20-20-4.png" data-ba=
se-url=3D"https://wiki.one.int.sap/wiki" data-linked-resource-content-type=
=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"2966325080" data-linked=
-resource-container-version=3D"212" tabindex=3D"0" alt=3D"" height=3D"287">=
</span></p>
<p>Input data for RAP actions can be defined per step in JSON format. The J=
SON data allows the user to define test data for any RAP BO without the nee=
d for a Test Data Container or dictionary objects. There are no prerequisit=
es, nothing needs to be transported except the script itself. For steps on =
RAP BOs that require input data beyond a referenceStep, the user has to def=
ine the data as JSON. Typically, the user will just fill values into the te=
mplate JSON that can be be generated right in the editor, specifically for =
the current RAP BO and Action.</p>
<p>No TDCs, and no entries in DB tables PTFBO and PTFBOA are needed for RAP=
 BOs. For them, value helps, validation and data access all work genericall=
y. PTF evaluates the metadata and uses dynamic EML.</p>
<h3 id=3D"PTFRAPAccess-JSONdatainPTFscripts">JSON data in PTF scripts</h3>
<p>The syntax used to access RAP with PTF is described in this wiki. The sy=
ntax is case <strong>in</strong>sensitive. However, the templates and the P=
retty Printer use camel case as much as possible.</p>
<p>Outside of double quotes, you can add spaces and line breaks at will, th=
ey will be ignored when JSON is parsed. Usage of " (double quotes) is manda=
tory for both property names and values. Only for values, if they are numer=
ic, or Boolean values, they are optional.</p>
<p>The ALV has been enhanced with a new column, left of column "Document ID=
". It contains a small button per step, which opens an editor to maintain s=
tep specific input in JSON format. The button is enabled only for RAP BOs a=
nd after an action has been chosen for the step.&nbsp;When the user presses=
 the button an editor window opens. It is prefilled with a suitable JSON te=
mplate, specific for BO and operation.</p>
<p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-manu=
al-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image" draggable=3D"false" heigh=
t=3D"253" src=3D"2947f75079a6d00d359b896eaa0bcdcada81de83d7ebe5f2c50ec84807=
f878bc" data-image-src=3D"/wiki/download/attachments/2966325080/image2022-8=
-1_12-57-9.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1659351430000&amp;api=3Dv=
