6" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachme=
nt" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image2022-8-1_12-57-56.png" data-=
base-url=3D"https://wiki.one.int.sap/wiki" data-linked-resource-content-typ=
e=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"2966325080" data-linke=
d-resource-container-version=3D"212" tabindex=3D"0" alt=3D"" height=3D"71">=
</span></p>
<p>For CREATE, CHANGE and CHECK the editor has the following buttons:</p>
<p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-manu=
al-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image" draggable=3D"false" heigh=
t=3D"26" src=3D"417e2a0c7f4af36537a682508783e01e274d1f77f2b1e5b7fe1f5cb8820=
7d1b6" data-image-src=3D"/wiki/download/attachments/2966325080/image2022-7-=
28_16-56-56.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1659016614000&amp;api=3D=
v2" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"30277178=
86" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachm=
ent" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image2022-7-28_16-56-56.png" dat=
a-base-url=3D"https://wiki.one.int.sap/wiki" data-linked-resource-content-t=
ype=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"2966325080" data-lin=
ked-resource-container-version=3D"212" tabindex=3D"0" alt=3D"" width=3D"468=
"></span></p>
<p>For RETRIEVE_ALL, the editor has the following buttons:</p>
<p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-manu=
al-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image" draggable=3D"false" heigh=
t=3D"33" src=3D"7340cb96ff28f4a000720f4d4015e175ad22580e3c0470b273b25bfa174=
2ed42" data-image-src=3D"/wiki/download/attachments/2966325080/image2022-10=
-19_11-34-28.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1666168459000&amp;api=
=3Dv2" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"31556=
34804" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"atta=
chment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image2022-10-19_11-34-28.png"=
 data-base-url=3D"https://wiki.one.int.sap/wiki" data-linked-resource-conte=
nt-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"2966325080" data=
-linked-resource-container-version=3D"212" tabindex=3D"0" alt=3D"" width=3D=
"416"></span></p>
<p>For DELETE, RETRIEVE, CHECK_IF_EXISTS, ENTITY_ACTIONS, and RAP Actions o=
f the root entity, the editor has the following buttons:</p>
<p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-manu=
al-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image confluence-thumbnail" drag=
gable=3D"false" height=3D"32" src=3D"cd2a80bd231feade354c264cedac2b50f8eecb=
ed6c28046220613a67a21c8543" data-image-src=3D"/wiki/download/attachments/29=
66325080/image2022-6-8_15-33-32.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1654=
691612000&amp;api=3Dv2" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-res=
ource-id=3D"2966692327" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-reso=
urce-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image2022-6-=
8_15-33-32.png" data-base-url=3D"https://wiki.one.int.sap/wiki" data-linked=
-resource-content-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"2=
966325080" data-linked-resource-container-version=3D"212" tabindex=3D"0" al=
t=3D"" width=3D"294"></span></p>
<ul>
 <li>Continue: takes over the JSON as part of the PTF script (it will be sa=
ved together with the script when the script is saved later); but first it =
validates the JSON and issues a success message if JSON is valid or an erro=
r message with source position if the JSON is not valid;</li>
 <li>Pretty Printer: pretty prints the JSON data and applies camelCase to e=
ntity names and actions</li>
 <li>Template: No Fields: regenerates sample JSON without fields</li>
 <li>Template: Mandatory and Key Fields: regenerates sample JSON with key a=
nd mandatory fields</li>
 <li>Template: Key Fields: regenerates sample JSON with all key fields</li>
 <li>Template: All Fields: regenerates sample JSON with all fields</li>
 <li>Get JSON Template: regenerates sample JSON with all possible needed fi=
elds (similar to 'Template: All Fields')</li>
 <li>Clear: Deletes the whole text in the editor</li>
 <li>Cancel: Closes the editor without saving</li>
</ul>
<p>Maintained JSON data at a step can be persisted as part of the PTF scrip=
t. If the user maintains JSON data and presses button "Continue", the butto=
n changes its icon to indicate that data has been saved. Cells "Variant" an=
d "Testdata Container" become read-only since no TDC is needed if the user =
wants to use JSON data as input for the current step.</p>
<p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-manu=
al-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image" draggable=3D"false" heigh=
t=3D"29" src=3D"a36f91540ad0b4ed7c269fa2acab268bb219219f47a9c3d2262a318879a=
a592a" data-image-src=3D"/wiki/download/attachments/2966325080/image2022-8-=
1_11-0-31.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1659344431000&amp;api=3Dv2=
" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"3046573250=
" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachmen=
t" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image2022-8-1_11-0-31.png" data-ba=
se-url=3D"https://wiki.one.int.sap/wiki" data-linked-resource-content-type=
=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"2966325080" data-linked=
-resource-container-version=3D"212" tabindex=3D"0" alt=3D"" width=3D"468"><=
/span></p>
<h4 id=3D"PTFRAPAccess-JSONTemplates">JSON Templates &nbsp;</h4>
<p>A (BO and Action specific) template is generated if you open the JSON ed=
itor for a step which does not have a JSON string yet.&nbsp;You can also tr=
igger the creation of the template again, with different levels of details.=
</p>
<p>The JSON templates do not propose any values for the node properties but=
 use the value field to inform whether a field is a key field, mandatory (a=
ccording to behavior definition), or optional. To fully create an object, t=
here might be more fields mandatory than the behavior definition describes.=
</p>
<h3 id=3D"PTFRAPAccess-Remarks">Remarks&nbsp;</h3>
<ul>
 <li>Reference Steps in the PTF script (to previous steps) overrule the key=
 values given in JSON. This works also for parts of the key, if several key=
 fields exist.</li>
 <li>Mixing RAP BOs and traditional PTF BOs in the same script is absolutel=
y possible.</li>
 <li>Note that RAP BOs, like BAPIs, basically expect field values in the in=
ternal SAP format (e.g., with leading zeroes), not in the external format. =
(Reasoning <span style=3D"color:#0c66e4;"><a href=3D"https://blogs.sap.com/=
2022/06/27/conversion-exits-and-the-abap-restful-application-programming-mo=
del-rap/" class=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow">here</a>)</span>. In cer=
tain cases (ALPHA(numerical values) , ISOLA(language codes) ) PTF applies a=
n automatic conversion via conversion exit, but standard is to provide the =
data in JSON in the internal format.</li>
 <li>Objects with multiple key fields are fully supported. Between actions =
of RAP BOs, the keys can be transferred as usual, e.g., via reference step.=
 Also, traditional PTF BO Actions can consume objectIDs with multiple key f=
ields, by using method CL_PTF_RUN=E2=86=92GET_RESULT_KEY_DATA( ) to get a t=
yped structure. Alternatively, a pipe (|) is used in the char70 object ID f=
ield to separate the key fields.</li>
</ul>
<h4 id=3D"PTFRAPAccess-ValuehelpforActions">Value help for Actions</h4>
<p>The value help for RAP Actions is of course BO specific. Action CREATE w=
ill be listed only if either the root entity or at least one of the child e=
ntities are enabled for creation (as per class CL_ABAP_BEHV_LOAD, method GE=
T_LOAD). The same rule applies also for CHANGE and DELETE. The method is li=
sted even if the root entity is not enabled for creation but at least one o=
f the child entities is.</p>
<h3 id=3D"PTFRAPAccess-JSONSchema">JSON Schema</h3>
<p>Please check the following <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JSON=
" class=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow">Wikipedia page</a> for more deta=
ils about JSON.</p>
<p>The JSON schema usually has the following properties more or less used f=
or each possible Action and represents basically the same hierarchy with th=
e same relationships as the one described in the RAP Behavior Definition.</=
p>
<ul>
 <li><strong>_comment</strong>: A comment that better explains the purpose =
of the JSON.</li>
 <li><strong>fields</strong>: An array where the user can insert the fields=
 that wants to use for an Entity (Root and / or Child); Each element in an =
array is also represented by another object that usually has two properties=
: <strong>name&nbsp;</strong>which stores the name of the field of an Entit=
y and <strong>value </strong>which holds the value of the field (directly w=
ritten or as reference). In the property <strong>value </strong>the user ca=
n see some already prefilled "dummy" values to hint if the field is a key f=
ield or mandatory or optional. <br>
   There is another optional property on this level:</li>
</ul>
<ul>
 <li style=3D"list-style-type: none;">
  <ul>
   <li><strong>operator,</strong> with default value "=3D", used for Action=
 CHECK, this allows one of the following Boolean operators: =3D, &lt;&gt;, =
&gt;, &gt;=3D, &lt;, &lt;=3D&nbsp;</li>
  </ul></li>
</ul>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 40.0px;">There is also the possibility to use a mo=
re simplified syntax as exemplified below.</p>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 40.0px;">Normal syntax for "fields" property:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
 <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
  <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"bru=
sh: json; gutter: false">{"_comment":"JSON Create Example for RAP BO R_Prod=
uctionSupplyAreaTP - standard format"
 ,"fields":[
=09{"name":"ProductionSupplyArea","value":"TEST_ARE01"},
=09{"name":"Plant","value":"0001"},
=09{"name":"StorageLocation","value":"0001"}
 ]
=20
,"associations":[
=09{"childEntityName":"R_ProductionSupplyAreaTextTP","assocName":"_PRODUCTI=
ONSUPPLYAREATEXT" ,"fields":[
=09=09{"name":"Language","value":"EN"},
=09=09{"name":"ProductionSupplyAreaName","value":"Test Area EN"}
=09    =09]
    },
=09{"childEntityName":"R_ProductionSupplyAreaTextTP","assocName":"_PRODUCTI=
ONSUPPLYAREATEXT" ,"fields":[
=09=09{"name":"Language","value":"DE"},
=09=09{"name":"ProductionSupplyAreaName","value":"Test Area DE"}
=09    =09]
    }
 ]

}</pre>
 </div>
</div>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 40.0px;">Simplified syntax for "fields" property (=
note the difference after "fields"):</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
 <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
  <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"bru=
sh: json; gutter: false">{"_comment":"JSON Create Example for RAP BO R_Prod=
uctionSupplyAreaTP - simplified format"
,"fields":
    {"ProductionSupplyArea":"TEST_ARE01",
=09 "Plant":"1010",
=09 "StorageLocation":"101A"}
,"associations":[
=09{"childEntityName":"R_ProductionSupplyAreaTextTP","assocName":"_PRODUCTI=
ONSUPPLYAREATEXT"
=09=09,"fields":
=09=09=09{"Language":"E",
=09=09=09 "ProductionSupplyAreaName":"Test Area EN"}
    },
=09{"childEntityName":"R_ProductionSupplyAreaTextTP","assocName":"_PRODUCTI=
ONSUPPLYAREATEXT"
=09=09,"fields":
        =09{"Language":"D",=20
=09=09=09 "ProductionSupplyAreaName":"Test Area DE"}
    }
  ]
}</pre>
 </div>
</div>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 40.0px;">This simplified form could be especially =
helpful if the user wants to copy/paste data from an oData JSON request. Th=
e simplified form does not support properties on field level (e.g. property=
 "operator").</p>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 40.0px;"><br></p>
<ul>
 <li><strong>associations:&nbsp;</strong>An array that stores the associati=
ons of the parent entity. A new association is composed again of fields and=
 possibly an array of other associations and so on... Each association has =
the following properties:</li>
 <li><strong>childEntityName:&nbsp;</strong>The name of the Child Entity. N=
ote: we do not have a JSON property for the root entity name because for th=
e names of the root entity we use the name from the cell "Business Object" =
at step level.</li>
 <li><strong>assocName</strong>: The name of the association.</li>
</ul>
<p>Other properties found in the 1st level:</p>
<ul>
 <li><strong>commit</strong>: By default, this property has value "true" if=
 it's not mentioned in the JSON data. If the user explicitly mentions it in=
 the JSON with value false then the EML instruction to do the COMMIT and en=
d the RAP LUW is not called. This means that the user can bundle together m=
ultiple PTF steps in one RAP LUW and at the end use action COMMIT to end th=
e LUW.</li>
 <li><strong>skipInstanceFCEval</strong>: By default, this property has val=
ue "false" if it's not mentioned in the JSON data. If set to true, PTF itse=
lf will not check the operations against instance based feature control on =
field level before executing the EML call (note that the feature control by=
 the RAP BO during modify is not affected!). This is beneficial if you want=
 to test the RAP BOs feature control during modify. And also if you know th=
at the instance based feature control is not working correctly, e.g. in Sal=
esOrder update, where incorrect values are returned.</li>
 <li><strong>simulation:&nbsp;</strong>By default, this property has value =
"false" if it's not mentioned in the JSON data. If used with value "true" t=
han the EML instruction COMMIT ENTITIES will be called with the addition IN=
 SIMULATION MODE.</li>
 <li><strong>isDraft</strong>: If the entity is draft enabled this property=
 can mark the operation to be passed to the EML call as "draft".</li>
</ul>
<p>Properties found in both 1st level and other levels in the JSON data;</p=
>
<ul>
 <li><strong>ignore</strong>: By default, this property has value "false" i=
f it's not mentioned in the JSON data. If used with value "true" it skips t=
he entity to be passed to the EML call. The key fields still are passed to =
its children if an<strong> </strong>association to a child is given to spar=
e that common key fields have to be repeated. (Add earlier that child nodes=
 can leave out key fields common with their parent.)</li>
 <li><strong>isExisting</strong>: By default, this property has value "true=
" if it's not mentioned in the JSON data. Used only for action CHECK_IF_EXI=
STS, in case you want to validate that something is NOT there.</li>
 <li><strong>action</strong>: Mandatory property to name the action on chil=
d entity level in an ENTITY_ACTION step. For actions belonging to child ent=
ities PTF uses the generic action ENTITY_ACTION.</li>
 <li><strong>params:&nbsp;</strong>Holds the parameters that are passed to =
a RAP BO Action. 1:1 translation between JSON structure and ABAP structure =
/ hierarchy (e.g., if the parameters are a deep structure, then the JSON us=
ed as a value for this property also has to represent a deep JSON object). =
There is also the possibility to use a more simplified syntax as exemplifie=
d below.</li>
</ul>
<p>Normal syntax for "params" property, here used for a SalesOrder Action:<=
/p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
 <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
  <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"bru=
sh: json; gutter: false">{"_comment":"JSON Action Example for RAP BO R_Sale=
sOrderTP - action CreateWithReference - standard format",
"action":"CreateWithReference","fields":[],
=09"params":[
=09=09{"name":"SALESDOCUMENTTYPE","value":"TA"},
=09=09{"name":"REFERENCESDDOCUMENT","value":"1234"},
=09=09{"name":"_REFERENCESDDOCUMENTITEMS","value":[[
=09=09=09{"name":"REFERENCESDDOCUMENTITEM","value":"10"},
=09=09=09{"name":"REQUESTEDQUANTITY","value":"5"},
=09=09=09{"name":"REQUESTEDQUANTITYUNIT","value":"EA"}
=09=09=09]]
=09=09}
=09]
}</pre>
 </div>
</div>
<p>Simplified syntax for "params" property:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
 <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
  <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"bru=
sh: json; gutter: false">{"_comment":"JSON Action Example for RAP BO R_Sale=
sOrderTP - action CreateWithReference - simplified format",
 "action":"CreateWithReference",
 "fields":[],
 "params":{
=09=09=09"SALESDOCUMENTTYPE":"TA",
=09=09=09"REFERENCESDDOCUMENT":"1234",
=09=09=09"_REFERENCESDDOCUMENTITEMS":[
=09=09=09=09=09{
=09=09=09=09=09 "REFERENCESDDOCUMENTITEM":"10",
=09=09=09=09=09 "REQUESTEDQUANTITY":"5",
=09=09=09=09=09 "REQUESTEDQUANTITYUNIT":"EA"
=09=09=09=09=09}
            ]
  }
}</pre>
 </div>
</div>
<h5 id=3D"PTFRAPAccess-ReasoningbehindusingassociationsandassocNamealsoforC=
HANGEandDELETE">Reasoning behind using associations and assocName also for =
CHANGE and DELETE</h5>
<p>Even though the data in JSON is represented hierarchical, it is not alwa=
ys passed as a hierarchy to EML. The only actions where it would really be =
needed as a hierarchy would be for the CREATE action because here the data =
is translated into "Create by association" operations, and the RETRIEVE act=
ion because here the data is translated into "Read by association". However=
, for the sake of portability, avoiding repetition of key fields, and to qu=
ickly copy/paste the same JSON for different CRUD actions the user needs to=
 mention field "<strong>assocName</strong>" even for a child entity that is=
 used just for CHANGE of DELETE actions (even though the association name w=
ill not be used in the end in the EML operation that will be built and pass=
ed to the EML call).</p>
<h3 id=3D"PTFRAPAccess-OperationsforRAPBOs:">Operations for RAP BOs:</h3>
<h4 id=3D"PTFRAPAccess-CREATE">CREATE</h4>
<p>Creates a new root instance with optional child instances via "Create by=
 association". Can also create child instances for an existing parent insta=
nce.</p>
<p>Sample JSON for RAP BO R_SalesOrderTP that creates a root instance, one =
item and a specific item partner:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
 <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
  <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"bru=
sh: json; gutter: false">{ "_comment":"JSON Create",=E2=80=8B
"fields":[{"name":"SalesOrderType","value":"TA"},=E2=80=8B
    {"name":"SoldToParty","value":"0010100001"},=E2=80=8B
    {"name":"SalesOrganization","value":"1010"},=E2=80=8B
    {"name":"DistributionChannel","value":"10"},=E2=80=8B
    {"name":"OrganizationDivision","value":"00"},=E2=80=8B
    {"name":"PurchaseOrderByCustomer","value": "CreatedFromJsonInput"}],=E2=
=80=8B
    "associations":[{"childEntityName":"R_SalesOrderItemTP","assocName":"_I=
tem",=E2=80=8B
        "fields":[{"name":"Product","value":"TG11"},=E2=80=8B
        {"name":"Plant","value":"1010"},=E2=80=8B
        {"name":"RequestedQuantity","value":"2"}],=E2=80=8B
        "associations":[{"childEntityName":"R_SalesOrderItemPartnerTP","ass=
ocName":"_ItemPartner",=E2=80=8B
            "fields":[{"name":"PartnerFunctionForEdit","value":"WE"},=E2=80=
=8B
                      {"name":"Customer","value":"0010100004"}]=E2=80=8B
        }]=E2=80=8B
    }]=E2=80=8B
}</pre>
 </div>
</div>
<p>This example has been transported as PTF script <strong>DEMO_RAP_CREATE =
</strong>. It creates a SalesOrder on the database, using sComp master data=
 available e.g. in HBR.</p>
<p>To create a child entity for an existing instance, there is sample PTF s=
cript <strong>DEMO_RAP_ADD_CHILD_ENTITY&nbsp;</strong>, see step 2:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
 <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
  <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"bru=
sh: json; gutter: false">{"_comment":"JSON create)"
,"ignore":"true","fields":[{"name":"SalesOrder","value":"/Step[1]/%ResultId=
[1]"}]
,"associations":[
=09{"childEntityName":"R_SalesOrderItemTP","assocName":"_Item"
=09   ,"fields":[
=09=09=09=09{"name":"Product","value":"TM5_FERT01"},
=09=09=09=09{"name":"Plant","value":"0001"},
=09=09=09=09{"name":"RequestedQuantity","value":"5"}
=09   ]
=09}
]}</pre>
 </div>
</div>
<h4 id=3D"PTFRAPAccess-CHANGE">CHANGE</h4>
<p>Change root entity and / or child entities. (We know RAP itself uses the=
 term 'update', but PTF has been using CHANGE actions for years and a PTF s=
cript should be consistent between RAP BOs and non RAP BOs.)</p>
<p>Sample JSON for RAP BO R_SalesOrderTP that changes an text on root level=
, as well as, for item 000010, the Requested Quantity to 4:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
 <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
  <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"bru=
sh: json; gutter: false">{ "_comment":"Update root and one item",=E2=80=8B
"skipInstanceFCEval":true,
"fields":[{"name":"PurchaseOrderByCustomer","value": "UpdatedFromJsonInput"=
}],=E2=80=8B
    "associations":[{"childEntityName":"R_SalesOrderItemTP","assocName":"_I=
tem",=E2=80=8B
        "fields":[{"name":"SalesOrderItem",   "value":"000010"},=E2=80=8B
                  {"name":"RequestedQuantity","value":"4"     }]=E2=80=8B
    }]=E2=80=8B
}</pre>
 </div>
</div>
<p>You may check PTF script <strong>DEMO_RAP_CHANGE </strong>. It creates a=
 SalesOrder on the database, and then changes it in step 2, including an im=
plicit commit.&nbsp;</p>
<p>As BO SalesOrder (and other GOAL based SalesDocument BOs) has problems i=
n the instance permissions it returns in update case, here we deactivate PT=
F's instance permission handling with property<strong> </strong>skipInstanc=
eFCEval.</p>
<p>See also PTF script <strong>DEMO_RAP_CHANGE_2 </strong>that uses another=
 RAP BO.</p>
<h4 id=3D"PTFRAPAccess-DELETE">DELETE</h4>
<p>Deletes full objects or child entities. Only key fields have to be menti=
oned.</p>
<p>Sample JSON for RAP BO R_ProductionSupplyAreaTP that deletes an object i=
nstance (note that this BO has two key fields on root level. This example h=
as been transported as PTF script <strong>DEMO_RAP_DELETE</strong>):</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
 <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
  <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"bru=
sh: json; gutter: false">{"_comment":"JSON Delete Example for RAP BO R_PROD=
UCTIONSUPPLYAREATP",
"fields":[
=09{"name":"ProductionSupplyArea","value":"TEST_ARE01"},
=09{"name":"Plant","value":"0001"}
]}</pre>
 </div>
</div>
<p>To delete dedicated child entities, specify the nodes to be deleted, inc=
luding their parents up to the root node. Parent nodes that are mentioned b=
ut shall not be deleted can be excluded with property "ignore":true . See <=
strong>DEMO_RAP_DELETE_CHILD_ENTITY</strong> :</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
 <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
  <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"bru=
sh: json; gutter: false">{"_comment":"Delete child entity"
 ,"ignore":true
 ,"fields":[
=09{"name":"ProductionSupplyArea","value":"TEST_ARE01"},
=09{"name":"Plant","value":"1010"}]
 ,"associations":[
=09{"childEntityName":"R_ProductionSupplyAreaTextTP","assocName":"_PRODUCTI=
ONSUPPLYAREATEXT","ignore":false
      ,"fields":[
=09=09{"name":"ProductionSupplyArea","value":"TEST_ARE01"},
        {"name":"Plant","value":"1010"},
=09=09{"name":"LANGUAGE","value":"D"}
=09]}
]}</pre>
 </div>
</div>
<p>DELETE can also be used without JSON. If a reference step is defined for=
 the DELETE step, this is sufficient input (if you want to delete the whole=
 object).</p>
<h4 id=3D"PTFRAPAccess-CHECK">CHECK</h4>
<p>Compares field values of root entity and / or child entities against (fi=
xed or dynamic) expected values.&nbsp;</p>
<p>Optionally you can use property <strong>operator</strong>,<span> which s=
upports the</span> following Boolean operators: =3D, &lt;&gt;, &gt;, &gt;=
=3D, &lt;, &lt;=3D . If the property is not given, CHECK checks for equalit=
y.</p>
<p>Full keys are required (key values might come from ALV reference step, b=
e written in JSON(statically or as references), or for common key fields mi=
ght be inherited automatically from parent instances.</p>
<p>The given attribute values are checked against the instance that the key=
 field values specify.</p>
<p>Sample JSON for RAP BO R_SalesOrderTP that checks that the Requested Qua=
ntity of item 000010 is 3:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
 <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
  <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"bru=
sh: json; gutter: false">{"_comment":"JSON Check",=E2=80=8B
"fields":[{"name":"SalesOrder","value":"/Step[1]/%ResultId[1]"}],=E2=80=8B
=09"associations":[=E2=80=8B{"childEntityName":"R_SalesOrderItemTP","assocN=
ame":"_Item",=E2=80=8B
    =09"fields":[{"name":"SalesOrderItem","value":"000010"},=E2=80=8B
        =09      {"name":"RequestedQuantity","value":"3","operator":"=3D"}]=
=E2=80=8B
     }]=E2=80=8B
}</pre>
 </div>
</div>
<p>You may check PTF script <strong>DEMO_RAP_CHECK </strong>.</p>
<h4 id=3D"PTFRAPAccess-CHECK_IF_EXISTS">CHECK_IF_EXISTS</h4>
<p>Checks the existence of root entity and / or child entities. As the exis=
tence of entities is checked, normally only key fields have to be mentioned=
. (If you do not use 'free search', all non key fields are ignored.)</p>
<p>CHECK_IF_EXISTS can also be used without JSON. If a reference step is de=
fined for the CHECK_IF_EXISTS step, and the existence of the whole objects =
shall be validated, this is sufficient input.</p>
<p>See also property <strong>isExisting</strong>, that allows to use CHECK_=
IF_EXISTS for the opposite case, where you want to validate that an instanc=
e is NOT there.</p>
<p>Free search:&nbsp;Instead of specifying a BO instance by providing the f=
ull root key (in JSON or by reference step) you can also use 'free search'.=
 This means to identify BO instance(s) indirectly using non key attributes =
or incomplete keys. See also section 'Free search instead of reading by key=
'. If CHECK_IF_EXISTS uses free search, the check is successful if at least=
 one BO instance is found. (Existence validation of child entities is not p=
ossible with free search. But child entities can be used for input to ident=
ify BO instances.) If free search is used, property <strong>isExisting</str=
ong> is not supported and will be ignored.</p>
<p>See sample JSON for RAP BO R_ProductionSupplyAreaTP that checks the exis=
tence of the root entity and of two child entities R_ProductionSupplyAreaTe=
xtTP with the fully specified keys:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
 <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
  <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"bru=
sh: json; gutter: false">{"_comment":"JSON Existence Check Example for RAP =
BO R_ProductionSupplyAreaTP with key in parent",
"fields":[{"name":"ProductionSupplyArea","value":"TEST_ARE01"},{"name":"Pla=
nt","value":"0001"}],"associations":[
=09{"childEntityName":"R_ProductionSupplyAreaTextTP","assocName":"_PRODUCTI=
ONSUPPLYAREATEXT","ignore":"false","fields":[{"name":"Language","value":"E"=
}]},
=09{"childEntityName":"R_ProductionSupplyAreaTextTP","assocName":"_PRODUCTI=
ONSUPPLYAREATEXT","ignore":"false","fields":[{"name":"Language","value":"D"=
}]}
]}</pre>
 </div>
</div>
<p>You may check PTF script <strong>DEMO_RAP_CHECK_IF_EXISTS </strong>.</p>
<h4 id=3D"PTFRAPAccess-RETRIEVE_ALL">RETRIEVE_ALL</h4>
<p>There are two "RETRIEVE*" operations, RETRIEVE and RETRIEVE_ALL. Their p=
urpose is to load objects that can then be used as target for references (t=
o their fields) in later steps. Note that CHECK* operations retrieve the cu=
rrent data automatically and do not need a "RETRIEVE*" step (except if you =
want to compare the current data against dynamic data).</p>
<p>RETRIEVE_ALL reads all instances of all nodes of a Business Object. It i=
s even mass enabled, it can read multiple instances of the same Business Ob=
ject Type (when using free search).</p>
<p>Simple example: In example PTF script <strong>DEMO_RAP_RETRIEVE_ALL</str=
ong> step 3 creates a second SalesOrder, using some values of the first Sal=
esOrder which has been read with RETRIEVE_ALL in step 2:</p>
<p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-manu=
al-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image" draggable=3D"false" heigh=
t=3D"62" src=3D"2f9216d71b4459a78a513be9e27aa9967f0d335d6089b6eeae000a649ee=
7630d" data-image-src=3D"/wiki/download/attachments/2966325080/image2022-8-=
1_16-11-9.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1659363070000&amp;api=3Dv2=
" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"3046509380=
" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachmen=
t" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image2022-8-1_16-11-9.png" data-ba=
se-url=3D"https://wiki.one.int.sap/wiki" data-linked-resource-content-type=
=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"2966325080" data-linked=
-resource-container-version=3D"212" tabindex=3D"0" alt=3D"" width=3D"468"><=
/span></p>
<p>Step 2 uses no JSON but imports the DocumentID from its reference step.<=
/p>
<p>Step 3 defines in JSON several references to the SO retrieved in step 2.=
 The found values are used as input for the CREATE of the second SO (see <e=
m>Reference to object ID</em> for more details):&nbsp;</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
 <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
  <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"bru=
sh: json; gutter: false">{"_comment":"JSON Create - using fixed values, and=
 references to data fields of another SO instance, and a reference to a res=
ultID"
,"fields":[
    {"name":"SalesOrderType","value":"/Step[2]/R_SalesOrderTP/SALESORDERTYP=
E"},
    {"name":"SoldToParty","value":"/Step[2]/R_SalesOrderTP/SOLDTOPARTY"},
    {"name":"SalesOrganization","value":"/SteP[2]/R_SalesOrderTP/SALESORGAN=
IZATION"},
    {"name":"DistributionChannel","value":"/Step[2]/R_SalesOrderTP/DISTRIBU=
TIONCHANNEL"},
    {"name":"OrganizationDivision","value":"/Step[2]/R_SalesOrderTP/ORGANIZ=
ATIONDIVISION"},
    {"name":"PurchaseOrderByCustomer","value":"/Step[1]/%ResultId[1]"}],
    "associations":[
=09{"childEntityName":"R_SalesOrderItemTP","assocName":"_Item","fields":[
                {"name":"Product","value":"/Step[2]/R_SalesOrderTP/R_SalesO=
rderItemTP[1]/PRODUCT"},
                {"name":"Plant","value":"/Step[2]/R_SalesOrderTP/R_SalesOrd=
erItemTP[1]/PLANT"},
                {"name":"RequestedQuantity","value":"5"}
                ]}
    ]}
]}</pre>
 </div>
</div>
<p>RETRIEVE_ALL can use the full root key (given in JSON(statically or as r=
eference) or from reference step) to identify an instance. (This will be no=
ted with the message 'As full key is given for root entity, EML Read is don=
e with key access (free search not required)' in the log.) In this case, it=
 is possible to use RETRIEVE_ALL without JSON. If a reference step is defin=
ed for the RETRIEVE_ALL step, this is sufficient input (see example above, =
step 2). For access with full root key, JSON is needed only if as value of =
a key field a fixed ID shall be used, or if as value(s) of the root key one=
 of several objects keys from the reference step shall be chosen via index =
<em>IndexOfDocumentID of %ResultId</em>.</p>
<p>Or, for more complex cases, non key fields (of root entity and / or chil=
d entities) can be used. (And for keys with multiple fields, filling a subs=
et of key fields is also possible. Key fields and non key fields can be com=
bined freely. ) The log notes this with message 'Root keys not given, using=
 free search instead'. This can even lead to multiple objects being retriev=
ed. See also section '<em>Free search instead of reading by key</em>'.</p>
<p>For access without full key, of course, JSON is needed.</p>
<p>Here a sample code for Free Search that reads instances of R_SalesOrderT=
P by SalesOrder header field OrderType and SalesOrder Partner fields Partne=
rFunction and Customer. Selection is done with a logical AND:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
 <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
  <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"bru=
sh: json; gutter: false">{"_comment":"JSON Retrieve All Example for RAP BO =
R_SalesOrderTP"
,"fields":[
=09{"name":"SalesOrderType","value":"TA"}]
,"associations":[

=09{"childEntityName":"R_SalesOrderPartnerTP","assocName":"_PARTNER","field=
s":[
=09=09{"name":"PARTNERFUNCTION","value":"AG"},
=09=09{"name":"CUSTOMER","value":"0000000006"}
=09]}
]}</pre>
 </div>
</div>
<p>You may check PTF script <strong>DEMO_RAP_RETR_ALL_W_FREE_SRCH </strong>=
.</p>
<h4 id=3D"PTFRAPAccess-RETRIEVE">RETRIEVE</h4>
<p>RETRIEVE selects a subset of the entities of a single BO instance. Like =
with RETRIEVE_ALL the result is stored and can then be used as target for r=
eferences in later steps.</p>
<p>It is recommended to start with the root entity, you then have to specif=
y the full root key.</p>
<p>You have to mention the Entity (as childEntityName) and Association (as =
assocName) of whichever other entities shall be read. For these entities, k=
ey fields are only needed if you want to reduce the instances of this entit=
y. Keys can be left out. Partial keys can be used as well. Common key parts=
 will be inherited from the parent, as usual. Attribute fields (fields whic=
h are no key fields) have no use in RETRIEVE.</p>
<p>RETRIEVE can also be used without JSON. If a reference step is defined f=
or the RETRIEVE step, its result will specify the BO instance. Only the roo=
t entity would be stored then.</p>
<p>Sample JSON for RAP BO R_ProductionSupplyAreaTP that retrieves root enti=
ty and child entities R_ProductionSupplyAreaTextTP (PTF script DEMO_RAP_RET=
RIEVE step 2):</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
 <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
  <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"bru=
sh: json; gutter: false">{"_comment":"JSON Retrieve Example for RAP BO R_Pr=
oductionSupplyAreaTP, for the text node all existing records are read",
"fields":[{"name":"PRODUCTIONSUPPLYAREA","value":"TEST_ARE01"},{"name":"PLA=
NT","value":"0001"}],"associations":[
=09{"childEntityName":"R_ProductionSupplyAreaTextTP","assocName":"_PRODUCTI=
ONSUPPLYAREATEXT","ignore":"false",
        "fields":[{"name":"PRODUCTIONSUPPLYAREA","value":"TEST_ARE01"},{"na=
me":"PLANT","value":"0001"}]}
]}</pre>
 </div>
</div>
<p>The snippet above doesn't use a full key for node R_ProductionSupplyArea=
TextTP, so all child entities R_ProductionSupplyAreaTextTP of this BO insta=
nce will be read regardless of their language. The reason is that the EML r=
ead uses only the key of the parent entity, in our case the keys of the roo=
t entity R_ProductionSupplyareTP.</p>
<p>If you want to retrieve only one specific instance of a child node then =
you can mention the full key of the instance (here: two key fields from roo=
t, and text node key "Language"). The EML call will still read all the entr=
ies (of requested nodes) but only the instance matching the key will be kep=
t (and can be accessed in references from later steps). See PTF script DEMO=
_RAP_RETRIEVE, step 4</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
 <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
  <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"bru=
sh: json; gutter: false">{"_comment":"JSON Retrieve Example, specifying whi=
ch of the text node instances shall be read",
"fields":[{"name":"PRODUCTIONSUPPLYAREA","value":"TEST_ARE01"},{"name":"PLA=
NT","value":"1010"}],"associations":[
=09{"childEntityName":"R_ProductionSupplyAreaTextTP","assocName":"_PRODUCTI=
ONSUPPLYAREATEXT","ignore":"false",
         "fields":[{"name":"PRODUCTIONSUPPLYAREA","value":"TEST_ARE01"},{"n=
ame":"PLANT","value":"1010"},{"name":"Language","value":"E"}]}
]}</pre>
 </div>
</div>
<p>You may check PTF script <strong>DEMO_RAP_RETRIEVE </strong>.</p>
<h4 id=3D"PTFRAPAccess-ENTITY_ACTION">ENTITY_ACTION</h4>
<p>Executes one action of a child entity of the BO. (Root actions have dedi=
cated actions available in the value help.)</p>
<p>Note that the JSON templates that are generated for Action ENTITY_ACTION=
 do list all non-root actions of the BO, and you have to delete all but one=
.</p>
<p>Sample JSON for RAP BO R_SalesOrderTP, child entity R_SalesOrderShipToPa=
rtyTP, action ChangeAddress:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
 <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
  <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"bru=
sh: json; gutter: false">{"_comment":"JSON Action Example for RAP BO child =
entity",
"action":"ChangeAddress","childEntityName":"R_SalesOrderShipToPartyTP",
"fields":[{"name":"SalesOrder","value":"421"}],
"params":[{"name":"BusinessPartnerName1","value":"Name1"},
          {"name":"BusinessPartnerName2","value":"Name2"}]
}</pre>
 </div>
</div>
<p>You may check PTF script <strong>DEMO_RAP_ENTITY_ACTION </strong>.</p>
<h4 id=3D"PTFRAPAccess-COMMIT">COMMIT</h4>
<p>As standard behaviour, PTF will do a commit automatically for every chan=
ging RAP operation. For this, no dedicated COMMIT step is needed. See prope=
rty "commit" for details on implicit commit.</p>
<p>The following is the current behavior (workaround) that is likely to cha=
nge when we will offer own PTF actions for COMMIT WORK and COMMIT ENTITIES.=
&nbsp;</p>
<p>If you have at least one step with Action COMMIT for any RAP BO, the who=
le PTF script will run in one common internal session (instead of one per s=
tep), as explicit commits make only sense if a COMMIT step can commit somet=
hing transient from earlier steps. Note that a COMMIT confirms of course th=
e whole session, not only the RAP BO for which you select the COMMIT action=
. Precisely PTF action COMMIT executes a EML COMMIT ENTITIES, which include=
s COMMIT WORK for non RAP changes.</p>
<p>COMMIT does not use JSON.</p>
<p>You may check PTF script <strong>DEMO_RAP_COMMIT </strong>.</p>
<h4 id=3D"PTFRAPAccess-OtherinformationrelatedtoPTFRAPoperations">Other inf=
ormation related to PTF RAP operations</h4>
<p>All operations (except RETRIEVE_ALL and COMMIT) can be used on root enti=
ty as well as to work on sub nodes only.</p>
<p>Not all of these actions are offered for all RAP BOs. This depends on th=
e behaviour definition.</p>
<h4 id=3D"PTFRAPAccess-BOSpecificActions">BO Specific Actions</h4>
<p>Additionally, BO specific actions ( of the root entity ) are listed dire=
ctly in the Action F4 help, together with the standard operations ( CREATE,=
 CHECK, etc.). If the root action has no parameters, no JSON is needed.</p>
<p>To call actions of sub nodes (child entities), use action ENTITY_ACTION,=
 which always requires a JSON. Use property "action" in the step JSON to se=
t the action name.</p>
<p>For both root an subnode actions, property "params" is mandatory if the =
action has parameters.</p>
<p>RAP BO R_SalesOrderTP, action RemoveBillingBlock without JSON (as <stron=
g>without parameters</strong>), Step 3 in the screenshot below:</p>
