<h4 id=3D"PTFRAPAccess-Freesearchinsteadofreadingbykey"><span class=3D"inli=
ne-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"8b32ede6-ebe2-4c88-a470-598e7b1958e0">Free s=
earch instead of reading by key</span></h4>
<p>For RETRIEVE_ALL and CHECK_IF_EXISTS there is the possibility to use als=
o other fields instead of just the key fields of the root node. In case onl=
y an incomplete or no root key is provided (from JSON and/or reference step=
), a free search is executed based on the field values given in JSON. Root =
entity fields and fields from (multiple) child entities can be used togethe=
r. Given fields are always interpreted with a logical AND, i.e. only BO ins=
tances are found that meet all given field values of all given nodes. The a=
ccess can retrieve one or more instances when it's successful.</p>
<p>Free search is useful when a step shall access an instance or instances,=
 and the key values are unknown. The instances selected using free search c=
an then be referenced by later steps ( in case of RETRIEVE_ALL ) or their e=
xistence is validated in the same step ( in case of CHECK_IF_EXISTS ).</p>
<p>Note that the values of common key fields of parent nodes are not inheri=
ted in a free search.</p>
<p>Find a sample snippet below that could be used at RETRIEVE_ALL or CHECK_=
IF_EXISTS for RAP BO R_SalesOrderTP. A combination of key and non key field=
s of Root entity and child entities is being used instead of only key field=
s:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
 <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
  <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"bru=
sh: json; gutter: false">{"_comment":"JSON Retrieve All Example for RAP BO =
R_SalesOrderTP"
,"fields":[
=09{"name":"SalesOrderType","value":"TA"}]
,"associations":[
=09{"childEntityName":"R_SalesOrderPartnerTP","assocName":"_PARTNER","field=
s":[
=09=09{"name":"PARTNERFUNCTION","value":"WE"},
=09=09{"name":"CUSTOMER","value":"10005"}
=09]},
=09{"childEntityName":"R_SalesOrderItemTP","assocName":"_ITEM"
     ,"fields":[
=09=09{"name":"SALESORDERITEM","value":"000020"},
 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;{"name":"PRODUCT","value":"TG11"}]
=09,"associations":[
=09=09{"childEntityName":"R_SalesOrderScheduleLineTP","assocName":"_SCHEDUL=
ELINE","fields":[
=09=09=09{"name":"SALESORDERITEM","value":"000020"},
=09=09=09{"name":"DELIVERYDATE","value":"%SY-DATUM"}
&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; ]}
=09]}
]}</pre>
 </div>
</div>
<p>In this sample log, please notice the messages "Root keys not given, usi=
ng free search instead" and "Stored 2 instance(s) of type R_SALESORDERTP":<=
/p>
<p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-manu=
al-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image" draggable=3D"false" heigh=
t=3D"185" src=3D"b9d0b5583a03fcbfcbad359aad0d86f97efe6c796a50f1759d9879f023=
0eeda9" data-image-src=3D"/wiki/download/attachments/2966325080/image2022-1=
0-26_16-54-43.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1666792484000&amp;api=
=3Dv2" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"31696=
90014" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"atta=
chment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image2022-10-26_16-54-43.png"=
 data-base-url=3D"https://wiki.one.int.sap/wiki" data-linked-resource-conte=
nt-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"2966325080" data=
-linked-resource-container-version=3D"212" tabindex=3D"0" alt=3D"" width=3D=
"468"></span></p>
<h3 id=3D"PTFRAPAccess-InputvalidationsusedinRAPBOoperations">Input validat=
ions used in RAP BO operations</h3>
<p>PTF offers various automatic validation mechanisms to avoid a dump if th=
e final EML call with operations at step level is not done properly.</p>
<p>Some of the validations automatically done are:</p>
<ul style=3D"list-style-type: square;">
 <li>validate JSON data syntax</li>
 <li>validate mandatory fields and read-only fields based on global and ins=
tance permissions</li>
 <li>validate entity names, field names, parameter names, association names=
, action names, operations type (C/U/D), and draft enabling, against behavi=
or definition</li>
 <li>validate whether keys are filled</li>
 <li>validate that value conversion from JSON field properties (and paramet=
er properties) to RAP target entity fields (and parameters) does not fail</=
li>
</ul>
<p>There are some limited conversions done to the input data:</p>
<ul style=3D"list-style-type: square;">
 <li>conversion exits (if used at a fields domain) are applied (for conveni=
ence) if they are one of the following: ALPHA(for numerical values), ISOLA =
for language codes).&nbsp; &nbsp;(Currently there is a warning message in t=
he log, not an error message, if such a conversion exit fails). In general,=
 use the internal format in JSON.</li>
 <li>trim values that are longer than the target fields (a warning is writt=
en to the log)</li>
</ul>
<p>All the error messages or warning messages can be seen by clicking the "=
Application Log" button from the application toolbar.</p>
<h3 id=3D"PTFRAPAccess-Dynamicdata(References)">Dynamic data (References)</=
h3>
<p>In a PTF JSON string, most values will be literals, e.g. a static materi=
alID. Dynamic values are also supported.</p>
<ul>
 <li>You can reference objectIDs resulting from earlier steps.</li>
 <li>You can reference the content of any field of an object.</li>
 <li>You can reference the content of SYST fields.</li>
</ul>
<h4 id=3D"PTFRAPAccess-ReferencetoobjectID">Reference to object ID</h4>
<p>You can reference objectIDs that are returned by earlier steps, using ke=
yword <strong>%ResultId</strong></p>
<ul>
 <li>Any step before the current one can be used - designate with <strong>S=
tep[N]</strong> where N is the step number.</li>
 <li>Specify an index like %ResultId<strong>[2]</strong> if you expect mult=
iple objectIDs resulting from the step.</li>
 <li>If the BO of the referenced step has multiple key fields, they are all=
 addressed together as one resultID</li>
</ul>
<p>Syntax: &nbsp;</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
 <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
  <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"bru=
sh: java; gutter: false">/Step[StepNumber]/%ResultId[IndexOfDocumentID]&nbs=
p; &nbsp; </pre>
 </div>
</div>
<p><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">If no index is given, like in&nbs=
p; /Step[3]/%ResultId&nbsp; then Index [1] is used per default.</span></p>
<p>Example:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
 <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
  <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"bru=
sh: java; gutter: false">/Step[1]/%ResultId[1] &nbsp;</pre>
 </div>
</div>
<p>Log sample if reference was resolved successfully:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
 <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
  <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"bru=
sh: java; gutter: false">Entity R_SALESORDERITEMTP, field MATERIAL: Referen=
ce mapping
Referenced ResultID: 0003108478</pre>
 </div>
</div>
<h4 id=3D"PTFRAPAccess-Referencetoafieldofanobject">Reference to a field of=
 an object</h4>
<p>You can reference the content of any field of any node of any BO. Typica=
lly, a RETRIEVE or RETRIEVE_ALL is necessary to read the instance. You can =
then reference any field of the entities that have been read in the RETRIEV=
E* step. This works also for transient objects (not yet persisted) if they =
provide a PID.<br>
  If there are multiple instances of a node, e.g. document items, then spec=
ify one instance by index (example: /R_SALESORDERITEMTP[1] ) or by conditio=
n (attribute name and attribute value (with '=3D')). It is even possible to=
 link several conditions with with "and" and "or".</p>
<p>Syntax:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
 <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
  <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"bru=
sh: java; gutter: false">/Step[StepNumber]/RootEntity[optionalRecordIndex]/=
ChildEntity[optionalRecordIndex].../Fieldname</pre>
 </div>
</div>
<p>Example:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
 <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
  <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"bru=
sh: java; gutter: false">/Step[4]/R_SALESORDERTP[1]/R_SALESORDERITEMTP[1]/P=
RODUCT =E2=80=8B</pre>
 </div>
</div>
<p>Example with short form without index for the node instances (then we ta=
ke the first record):</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
 <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
  <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"bru=
sh: java; gutter: false">/Step[4]/R_SALESORDERTP/R_SALESORDERITEMTP/PRODUCT=
</pre>
 </div>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;Examples with attribute access, reading the quantity of a SalesOrd=
er Item:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
 <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
  <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"bru=
sh: java; gutter: false">"value":"/Step[1]/R_SALESORDERTP/R_SALESORDERITEMT=
P[product =3D 'TM5_FERT']/RequestedQuantity"
"value":"/Step[1]/R_SALESORDERTP/R_SALESORDERITEMTP[RequestedQuantity =3D '=
47' OR product =3D 'TM5_FERT']/RequestedQuantity</pre>
 </div>
</div>
<p>Note also the example PTF script described above at operation RETRIEVE_A=
LL.</p>
<p>The referenced value is also written in the log. Example log if referenc=
e was resolved successfully (Note that the field mentioned here is the name=
 of the target field, not the referenced field.):</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
 <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
  <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"bru=
sh: java; gutter: false">Entity R_SALESORDERTP, field SALESORDER: Reference=
 mapping&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;=20
Referenced value: TA</pre>
 </div>
</div>
<h4 id=3D"PTFRAPAccess-ReferencetoaSYSTfield/systemvariable.">Reference to =
a SYST field / system variable.</h4>
<p>You can use the value from any field of structure SYST. Also, addition a=
nd subtraction (only for date and time variables) are supported:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
 <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
  <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"bru=
sh: java; gutter: false">%SY-DATLO
%SY-DATLO + 365
%SY-DATLO+365
%SY-SYSID</pre>
 </div>
</div>
<h4 id=3D"PTFRAPAccess-Moreinfoonthereferences">More info on the references=
</h4>
<ul>
 <li>Index [1] can be omitted, it is used implicitly.</li>
 <li>A warning will be logged if the referenced value is longer than the ta=
rget field.</li>
 <li>For references to a data field, cardinality of reference records shoul=
d be 1. If attribute access is used, and there are multiple node entries ma=
tching the attributes, the first is used and a warning is written to the lo=
g, that includes the number of entries.</li>
 <li>All three kinds of references support offset and/or reduced length, li=
ke +2(10)&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;(note that this is not supported=
 for SYST fields, when they have date or time, as this conflicts with addit=
ion)</li>
 <li>Note that ReferenceSteps defined in the ReferenceStep column in the AL=
V have no effect on the references you define for individual fields in JSON=
. ReferenceSteps are on step level and are not related to these field speci=
fic references.</li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"PTFRAPAccess-PID/Latenumberingsupport">PID / Late numbering suppo=
rt</h3>
<p>For RAP objects with late numbering that have implemented preliminary id=
 logic handling, PTF supports transient CRUD operations on them. This means=
 that an uncommited step can return a PID instead of the permanent key. Lik=
e a normal key the PID is displayed in column DocumentID, and will be passe=
d to later steps that reference the current step. The PID can be addressed =
just like the permanent ID, with reference steps or reference variables. Pl=
ease observe in the next screenshot how for Step 1 the Document ID is actua=
lly a PID, and how after a commit the persistent key is returned in the Doc=
ument ID from by 3, representing the same BillingDocumentRequest:</p>
<p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-manu=
al-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image" draggable=3D"false" heigh=
t=3D"54" src=3D"3c8ecaf1c60ba91776b6568f690bd79008870c4285137d86933369b7472=
d0c5b" data-image-src=3D"/wiki/download/attachments/2966325080/image2022-6-=
9_13-5-40.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1654769138000&amp;api=3Dv2=
" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"2966466300=
" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachmen=
t" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image2022-6-9_13-5-40.png" data-ba=
se-url=3D"https://wiki.one.int.sap/wiki" data-linked-resource-content-type=
=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"2966325080" data-linked=
-resource-container-version=3D"212" tabindex=3D"0" alt=3D"" width=3D"468"><=
/span></p>
<h3 id=3D"PTFRAPAccess-AutomaticCIDhandling">Automatic CID handling</h3>
<p>For a CREATE operation EML expects also component CID to be filled. This=
 is automatically done by PTF, the value of the CIDs is composed with the f=
ollowing pattern:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
 <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
  <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"bru=
sh: java; gutter: false">C&lt;StepNumber&gt;&lt;InstanceNumber&gt;&lt;Incre=
mentalNumber&gt;</pre>
 </div>
</div>
<p>Details:</p>
<ul>
 <li>StepNumber : Value from column "Step"</li>
 <li>InstanceNumber: The order number of the instance in the JSON container=
 (currently only one Instance is supported per Step execution, so the value=
 is 1)</li>
 <li>IncrementalNumber: A number incremented for every entity instance, sta=
rting from root entity which has value 1 ( eg. If we have 1 root entity and=
 2 direct child entities, for the root entity we have value 1, and for the =
subsequent child entities we will have values 2, and 3 respectively)</li>
</ul>
<p>With all the information above we can determine that the first CID of a =
CREATE operation in Step 1 will be 'C111', the next one will be 'C112' havi=
ng as CID reference 'C111', and the next one will be 'C113' having as CID r=
eference 'C111'.</p>
